## Step 6 — Buyer Spec Audit

### Phase 1 — Top 2 RFQ Specs

Provided buyer specs: Structure Type (Fully Enclosed / Roof Only / Retractable Roof / 3-Side Covered), Roofing Material (Polycarbonate Sheet / Glass / Tensile Fabric / Color Coated Sheet), Frame Material (Aluminum / Galvanized Steel / Stainless Steel / Powder Coated Steel)

**Structure Type** (Fully Enclosed / Roof Only / Retractable Roof / 3-Side Covered): Defines the enclosure configuration — non-interchangeable. A seller supplying "Roof Only" structures cannot supply "Fully Enclosed." This is the primary routing spec — it determines which sellers can respond and at what price tier. **Rank 1.**

**Roofing Material** (Polycarbonate Sheet / Glass / Tensile Fabric / Color Coated Sheet): Defines the material system — non-interchangeable and drives the largest price variation. A tensile fabric specialist cannot substitute polycarbonate. Sellers need this to confirm capability and quote accurately. **Rank 2.**

### Phase 2 — Thumbnail Eligibility

**Structure Type:** Each value (Fully Enclosed / Roof Only / Retractable Roof / 3-Side Covered) represents a visually distinct enclosure configuration — these are recognisably different structures. **Thumbnail eligible: true.** Options: ["Fully Enclosed", "Roof Only", "Retractable Roof", "3-Side Covered"]

**Roofing Material:** Each value (Polycarbonate Sheet / Glass / Tensile Fabric / Color Coated Sheet) has a visually distinct appearance — polycarbonate is translucent, glass is clear/reflective, tensile fabric is membrane-like, colour coated sheet is opaque metal. **Thumbnail eligible: true.** Options: ["Polycarbonate Sheet", "Glass", "Tensile Fabric", "Color Coated Sheet"]

### Phase 3 — Missing Buyer Spec Audit

**Candidate gaps:**

- **Pool Dimensions / Area (sq ft):** Agent 3 confirms custom-fabricated to pool dimensions; sellers quote per sq ft. Without pool size, sellers cannot provide an accurate quote or confirm structural feasibility. Not present in buyer spec list under any name. → **Include. would_be_rank: 1** — more important than Structure Type because without dimensions, no seller can respond with a price. Not thumbnail eligible (numeric/dimensional).

- **Cover Type / Operational Mode** (Fixed / Retractable / Seasonal): Agent 3 identifies retractable as a distinct premium variant. The buyer spec "Retractable Roof" under Structure Type partially captures this, but the distinction between fixed and retractable is a primary cost driver that deserves its own spec. However — on semantic check, "Retractable Roof" IS present in Structure Type's top_values. This is already captured. → **Discard.**

- **Installation Location / Site Type** (New Pool / Existing Pool / Rooftop Pool): LLM world knowledge — sellers need to know if the pool is at ground level, on a rooftop, or indoors, as this affects structural design and installation complexity. Not present in buyer spec list. → **Include. would_be_rank: 2** — affects seller's ability to confirm feasibility and quote. Not thumbnail eligible (abstract site condition).

**Cross-reference check:**
- Pool Dimensions: not present ✓
- Installation Location: not present ✓

**Coverage verdict:** 2 missing specs → `partial`

**Image Upload Assessment:**
Swimming pool sheds are custom-fabricated to specific pool dimensions and site conditions. Buyers frequently have an existing pool with specific surrounding architecture, access constraints, or aesthetic requirements that cannot be captured in text specs alone. A photo of the pool site (showing pool dimensions, surrounding structure, access points) allows sellers to assess structural feasibility, identify installation challenges, and provide an accurate quote — without it, sellers must ask multiple follow-up questions before quoting. → `image_upload_recommended: true`

